h all around the world shows that  the more years kids are in school the  less motivated they  become  so so you know the starting point isn't  isn't a great one but of course there  are many things that that you can do and  and research on motivation has come a  long way too for example um if you are  surrounded by other people who are  motivated for something some of that  motivation can transfer to you that's  called motivation contagion um in in  psychology  and so  uh  you know expressing some enthusiasm  yourself uh with your kids for what  you're learning or teachers should keep  this in mind too if they are really  excited about what they're teaching  they can actually increase the  motivation in their students as well so  that's one thing we already talked about  i'll just jump in and say that um sal  always says the best way to communicate  excitement about something is to  actually be excited yourself about it  yeah that totally makes sense  and i couldn't agree more and  neuroscience supports it so  uh i mean that's great we already talked  about choice perhaps you cannot decide  you know what we need to do but but you  can give uh but students cannot decide  what to do but you can give them choice  in how to do it  um and we also know that mastery is very  important for learning uh that that that  students feel that they actually learn  and they they progress  so being a little bit  paying a little bit attention to  students needs and making sure they get  the help  to to to master new things is also very  important  because if students have too many bad  experiences in a row they might lose  faith in themselves and their abilities  to learn and then  they don't uh  expand they don't um spend any effort  and and then of course they don't learn  and then it's just a vicious circle  right yeah i i talk a lot about in  motivation research there's this idea of  um if you think that you'll be  successful when you do something it's a  lot more likely that you